{"id": "EUVD-2026-86040", "enisaUuid": "de6be797-ce23-3afc-9976-2bf4dc411e80", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/pm: bound pp_dpm_set_pp_table() memcpy\n\nThe powerplay path allocates hardcode_pp_table once with kmemdup(...,\nsoft_pp_table_size). memcpy(..., size) used the sysfs store count (up to\nPAGE_SIZE) with no upper bound, causing heap overflow. Reject\nwrites where size exceeds soft_pp_table_size.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:03:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:58:15", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/abe61d067b48b947bedc9bae3725cb8f48dc8c0a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9b5cb2e4eb297fe52be26fd895fc5ea28fc22bf9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/43d2ab8408f9f468b232350c74160ae21e763020", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3334985f8b4c7c637a829744c81518ad9a671bcb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f193e71fa9fab2e68ef85201b106e8f580d3a25b"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97427", "GHSA-797r-35j2-ppqg"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04ac3a23-fdc9-312c-842b-b5986d0f7168", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b9c1a77e8cd73aa42c2736b6b0ffddda6230af1a <3334985f8b4c7c637a829744c81518ad9a671bcb"}, {"id": "19af2ac3-b5c0-36a6-81d1-13cef4f86ed9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b9c1a77e8cd73aa42c2736b6b0ffddda6230af1a <43d2ab8408f9f468b232350c74160ae21e763020"}, {"id": "1d090ee5-c472-333f-b6e1-a0ea39b7aaa4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.6"}, {"id": "2ca36de9-830c-322b-8b9a-83ff34d8fdaa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "32a30b03-0871-35e3-9ef7-1ffd2cd76194", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b9c1a77e8cd73aa42c2736b6b0ffddda6230af1a <9b5cb2e4eb297fe52be26fd895fc5ea28fc22bf9"}, {"id": "395277e1-b4